==Battleground==
*3 [[Sir Rel]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>.
*1 [[Raynard]] spawns after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
*3 [[Sir Rel]]s spawn after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>, delay 6.67~10 seconds<sup>200f~300f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Camelle]] spawns as the boss.
**10 [[Sir Rel]]s spawn, delay 10~16.67 seconds<sup>300f~500f</sup>.
**35 [[Sir Rel]]s spawn, delay 2 seconds<sup>60f</sup>.
**3 [[Raynard]]s spawn, delay 53.33 seconds<sup>1,600f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Use [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Slapstick Cats]] to kill the Sir Rels and [[:Category:Wave Attack Cats|Wave Attackers]] like [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jellycat]] to deal damage to the Camelle. [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]] is also good for slowing Camelle and doing steady damage. Once all Sir Rels and the Camelle are dead, use a [[:Category:Rusher-class Cats|rusher]] like [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] to kill the Raynards and win.

As for other units who can work well here, [[Crazed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Island Cat]], [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Maglev Cat]], [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] can all help to kill the Sir Rels, while [[Cutter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Power Cutter Cat]] is more suited for killing Raynard. Camelle can really only be attacked once the Sir Rel wave dies down, so this is more of an endurance match. It is not recommended to use long-ranged units with somewhat low DPS such as [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|King Dragon Cat]] or the like, unless they are able to outrange Camelle. A high-level [[Sushi Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Roe Cat]] and [[:Category:Anti-Traitless Cats|anti-Traitless]] [[:Category:Tanker-class Cats|tankers]] can also be of use for the Raynards and Camelle, respectively.

==== <u>3 Crown Strategy</u> ====
On Three Crown, this stage ramps up from problematic to straight up near-impossible. The Sir Rels are ramped up extremely so, and the Raynards and Camelle prove to be formidable foes. It is recommended to use [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] to kill the Sir Rels at the start and gain enough cash from killing the singular Raynard. An extremely highly leveled Slapsticks Cat can help fend off the Sir Rels as well, with [[Ancient Egg: N000 (Special Cat)|Ape Lord Luza]] being capable of killing the Sir Rels in one shot at high levels. Wave Attackers like [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cat]] and [[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Macho Legs]] prove to be essential in chipping down Camelle. While [[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Esoteric Uril]] may seem like a good fit, his short range enables him to get sniped by Camelle extremely easily, so be careful with him. [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] can also be helpful in cleaning up the Raynards after Camelle has died. [[Maize Cat (Rare Cat)|Cone Cat]] can also be extremely useful as a meatshield. Finally, [[Elder Mask Doron (Special Cat)|Awakened Doron]] can be a vital asset as a last-resort nuke as well as a good way to chip Camelle.

Essentially, attempt to snipe Camelle while trying to stay alive in the process. Surge Immune units can work great as well, as they are less affected by Raynard's meddling.

==Trivia==
*This stage's name is a pun on Malaysia's capital, [[wikipedia:Kuala Lumpur|Kuala Lumpur]].
*Prior to [[Version 11.6 Update|version 11.6]], the boss fight had 4 Raynards instead of 3.

